 "result": "When `TESSEL_RUN_FROM_CLI == \"true\"`, `Tessel.run` does nothing and returns. The check is at `src/tessel/app.py:695-705`:\n\n- Unless it's running from the reloader (`is_running_from_reloader()`), it first prints a red warning: \" * Ignoring a call to 'app.run()' that would block the current 'tessel' CLI command. Only call 'app.run()' in an 'if __name__ == \"__main__\"' guard.\"\n- Then it does a bare `return`, so it never loads dotenv or starts a server.\n\nThe variable is set in `TesselGroup.make_context` at `src/tessel/cli.py:667`. That way an unguarded `app.run()` in the user's module doesn't start a second server and block whichever `tessel` command is being imported.",
